- **Height**: The height from \(H\) to the plane \(ABC\) (the \(xy\)-plane) is the \(z\)-coordinate of \(H\), which is 1.

Volume is \(\frac{1}{3} \times \text{base area} \times \text{height} = \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} \times 1 = \frac{1}{6}\).

Both methods confirm the volume of pyramid \(ABCH\) is \(\frac{1}{6}\).

